# Backup credentials (deploy/backup.env, mode 600, NOT sourced by the app).
# Keeping RESTIC_* / AWS_* out of .env means a web-app RCE cannot read the
# credential that deletes or encrypts the offsite repository.
# Quoting: RESTIC_PASSWORD and AWS_* below are forwarded from the script's
# environment (`-e VAR`), so normal quoting is fine. Any ADDITIONAL restic/AWS
# variable (e.g. RESTIC_CACHE_DIR, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION) reaches the container via
# `docker --env-file`, which does NOT strip quotes — leave those unquoted.
# Non-secret names the script also needs (same values as .env):
POSTGRES_USER=""
POSTGRES_DB=""
DATA_DIR=""
RESTIC_REPOSITORY=""
RESTIC_PASSWORD=""
# Config backup (T3-A): a SECOND repository with a DIFFERENT password. .env is
# never written to the data repository, so a leaked data repository and its
# password cannot decrypt BETTER_AUTH_SECRET / SUPPRESSION_HMAC_KEY / the DB
# password. Use a separate bucket (preferred) or a `/config` prefix; keep this
# password offline next to RESTIC_PASSWORD.
RESTIC_CONFIG_REPOSITORY=""
RESTIC_CONFIG_PASSWORD=""
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# Dedicated healthchecks.io check; pinged only on a successful backup.
BACKUP_PING_URL=""
# Separate weekly check (restic check) — silence here means integrity checks stopped.
CHECK_PING_URL=""
